/**
 * Sugar dynamics, carbon content, and transport properties.
 * Includes sugar concentration, carbon allocation, uptake, and flux.
 */
// Assume the sugar input is accumulated in the form of sucrose, 0.28 is the ssrat[1] concentration of glucose.
// Convert unit of sugar concentration from g sugar/g solution to mol sugar/mol solution.
// Example: Glucose (Glc) and Fructose (Fru) (180.2 g/mol) are major sugars accumulated in fruit. 
// There is Cgg g sugar (glucose) and (1 - Cgg) g water in 1 g solution with concentration Cgg g sugar/g solution;
// The calculation: Cmm (mol sugar/mol solution) = (Cgg/180.2) / (Cgg/180.2 + (1 - Cgg)/18), get Cmm = Cgg/(10 - 9Cgg)

public double sugarConcentration_fruit; /**< Soluble sugar concentration in the fruit (g soluble sugar/g water). */
